<title>UK: CRICKET-STATISTICAL COMPARISON OF ATHERTON AND MAY.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-STATISTICAL COMPARISON OF ATHERTON AND MAY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Atherton becomes England's longest-serving captain on Thursday when he leads his country against Australia at Lord's for the 42nd time in a test, beating Peter May's record of 41.</p>
<p>ATHERTON'S TEST MATCH RECORD</p>
<p>    Test matches:	 Batting record:</p>
<p>    Played    41	  Innings	     72</p>
<p>    Won	 11	  Not Out		3</p>
<p>    Drawn     17	  Runs	     3,143 </p>
<p>    Lost	13	  Highest score    185</p>
<p>				Average	  45.55</p>
<p>				100s		   8</p>
<p>Series results:</p>
<p>    Year    Opponents   Venue  Won  Lost  Drawn  Result</p>
<p>    1993    Australia    H	1    1     0	*</p>
<p>    1993-4  West Indies  A	1    3     1	Lost</p>
<p>    1994    New Zealand  H	1    0     2	Won</p>
<p>    1994    South Africa H	1    1     1	Drawn</p>
<p>    1994-5  Australia    A	1    3     1	Lost</p>
<p>    1995    West Indies  H	2    2     2	Drawn</p>
<p>    1995-6  South Africa A	0    1     4	Lost</p>
<p>    1996    India	  H	1    0     2	Won</p>
<p>    1996    Pakistan     H	0    2     1	Lost</p>
<p>    1996-7  Zimbabwe     A	0    0     2	Drawn</p>
<p>    1996-7  New Zealand  A	2    0     1	Won</p>
<p>    1997    Australia    H	1    0     0 </p>
<p>    TOTAL			    11   13    17    </p>
<p>* Atherton captained for last two tests of six-test series which was lost 4-1.</p>
